   "source": [
    "## 5. Preprocesamiento + K-Means (Paso 9.2 de la guía)\n",
    "\n",
    "Todo va dentro de un `Pipeline`, así las mismas transformaciones del entrenamiento se aplican automáticamente cuando Streamlit reciba un nuevo caso. `random_state=42` garantiza que los clusters sean los mismos cada vez que se entrena (reproducibilidad)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "0ec57d9b",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-11-04T11:46:43.756188Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-11-04T11:46:43.755892Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-11-04T11:46:44.577519Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-11-04T11:46:44.576724Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "0    1168\n",
       "1    1015\n",
       "2    1294\n",
       "Name: count, dtype: int64"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 7,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\n",
    "from sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "from sklearn.cluster import KMeans\n",
    "\n",
    "model = Pipeline([\n",
    "    (\"imputer\", SimpleImputer(strategy=\"median\")),\n",
    "    (\"scaler\", StandardScaler()),\n",
    "    (\"cluster\", KMeans(\n",
    "        n_clusters=3,\n",
    "        random_state=42,\n",
    "        n_init=\"auto\"\n",
    "    ))\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "labels = model.fit_predict(X)\n",
    "pd.Series(labels).value_counts().sort_index()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b5cdad81",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Evaluar estructura (Paso 9.3 de la guía)"
